se-cards/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/custom-laravel-pulse-cards-hcez4zvdo","summary":"Learn how to create custom Pulse cards in Laravel using the Fly.io platform and Pulse's Livewire component. Capture and display metrics such as requests per machine in your own custom Pulse card.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/57715d5eb856026b6cffcfcda03b49e3?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-13T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"msUDAI6Bm","title":"Monitoring Fly Machine Resource Usage with Laravel Pulse","url":"https://fly.io/laravel-bytes/laravel-pulse-machines/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/monitoring-fly-machine-resource-usage-with-laravel-pulse-msudai6bm","summary":"Learn how to monitor and display resource usage of Fly Machines running a Laravel app using Laravel Pulse's servers card.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9c1b01cc3dc2777b94c76aa4fb1f83b6?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"X4n6y4D2O","title":"Autoscaled Queue Workers","url":"https://fly.io/laravel-bytes/autoscaled-queue-workers/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/autoscaled-queue-workers-x4n6y4d2o","summary":"The article discusses the process of scaling queue workers using Fly.io and Laravel. It explains how Docker images are converted to Micro VM's, the purpose of the 'fly:work' console command in Laravel, and how scaled queue workers can be created using Fly Machines.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8e9eff0031f2a5f640876d788855e9d9?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-14T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"nFjkf3y05","title":"Streaming updates with Livewire and Fly Machines","url":"https://fly.io/laravel-bytes/streaming-fly-machines/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/streaming-updates-with-livewire-and-fly-machines-nfjkf3y05","summary":"The article discusses how to redirect long-running requests in a Laravel app to a separate instance called Tasker-Machine using Fly Machines. It explains the use of Livewire's `wire:stream` directive for streaming updates to the UI, the process of creating a Tasker-Machine with Fly Machines, and the implementation of middleware to redirect requests to the appropriate instance.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8d23c64fff9d5b4f36a3211abcc3995d?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-14T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"lSqCVzqTG","title":"Making the CLI and Browser Talk","url":"https://fly.io/laravel-bytes/making-the-cli-and-browser-talk/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/making-the-cli-and-browser-talk-lsqcvzqtg","summary":"The article discusses how to make the CLI and web browser interact in a Laravel application. It explains the process of CLI authentication, creating a CLI session, and checking the session status. The article also provides instructions for adjusting the browser-based registration flow to capture the CLI session ID. The author suggests using web sockets or starting a local web server as alternative methods for CLI-browser communication.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7e570628314f065a21d0341e878786cb?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"jhGaX8J2z","title":"Checkboxes, and Streamed updates with Livewire","url":"https://fly.io/laravel-bytes/checkboxes-streaming-livewire/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/checkboxes-and-streamed-updates-with-livewire-jhgax8j2z","summary":"The article discusses how to use Livewire's wire:stream directive to progressively update the UI, how to wire checkboxes to an array in Livewire, and the purpose of the process-stream receiver.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5c5d17146cb8e239924e8cc22abf8742?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"MJ01dPQ9w","title":"Livewire v3: Modelable, Events, and Data Sharing","url":"https://fly.io/laravel-bytes/modelable-events-data-livewire/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/livewire-v3-modelable-events-and-data-sharing-mj01dpq9w","summary":"This article discusses how to create dynamic, inter-dependent drop-downs in Laravel using Livewire. It explains how to uniquely identify each drop-down and share data between components. The Modelable attribute in Livewire is also introduced.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/faf97640bdcd6fafabe2aae58c7ed301?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"0dF9icswF","title":"Re-usable, Dependent Dropdowns in Livewire v3","url":"https://fly.io/laravel-bytes/dependent-dropdowns-livewire/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/re-usable-dependent-dropdowns-in-livewire-v3-0df9icswf","summary":"Re -usable, Dependent Dropdowns in Livewire v3 in Laravel v3 \u00b7 Laravel Bytes. How do we create dependency among dropdowns that use the same, re-usable component? One way we can solve this is by utilizing Livewire's powerful component nesting capabilities.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/548d3e69bbc89b505ad2b16b7c63398c?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-13T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"uPnSUPQwR","title":"Ad Hoc Tasks, GitHub Actions Style","url":"https://fly.io/laravel-bytes/ad-hoc-tasks/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ad-hoc-tasks-github-actions-style-upnsupqwr","summary":"Ad Hoc Tasks, GitHub Actions Style, and Laravel.io can be used to spin up a VM and run some code. Fly uses Docker images to create (real, non-container) VMs. Fly can only push images to Fly.io\u2019s registry for a specific app, e.g.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_au